            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Years</strong><br>\nGiuseppe Verdi was born on October 10, 1813, in Le Roncole, a small village in Italy. He was the son of an innkeeper and a spinner, showing musical talent at a very young age. He started to study music in the nearby town of Busseto.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Musical Education</strong><br>\nVerdi had his formal music education sponsored by a local patron and later moved to Milan. Although the Milan Conservatory rejected him, he took private lessons and became immersed in the city's vibrant musical life.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Early Career</strong><br>\nVerdi's first opera, \"Oberto,\" was performed in Milan in 1839 and achieved some success. This was followed by a series of operas, but it was \"Nabucco\" in 1842 that made him a star, especially due to its famous chorus \"Va, pensiero.\"</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
