          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Personal Tragedy and Recovery</strong><br>\nVerdi faced personal tragedy with the deaths of his wife and children early in his career. He found love again with the soprano Giuseppina Strepponi, who became his lifelong companion.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Death</strong><br>\nVerdi died on January 27, 1901. He left behind a legacy as one of the greatest opera composers of all time, with \"Requiem\" being one of his renowned non-operatic works.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Continuing Influence</strong><br>\nToday, Verdi's operas are performed worldwide, and his music is celebrated for its melodic brilliance, emotional depth, and dramatic intensity. His work has influenced generations of opera composers and continues to win over audiences with its timeless appeal.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
